@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema:  <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix cdi:     <http://ddialliance.org/Specification/DDI-CDI/1.0/RDF/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@base <https://www.ogc.org/rules/template/> .

# SHACL-NOT-APPLICABLE: permissive base with no root `required`; profiles add the shapes.
#
# geochemProduct is a JSON-Schema-driven base profile. Structural constraints are
# expressed in schema.yaml; no additional SHACL shapes are imposed at the generic
# base level (archive-specific profiles such as adaProduct add their own).
#
# Concretely: schema.yaml declares no root `required` list, so there is no obligation a
# NodeShape here could restate. Writing one would ASSERT constraints the JSON Schema does
# not make — e.g. demanding schema:distribution of every geochemProduct — and instances
# the schema calls valid would start failing SHACL. adaProduct, which does narrow the base,
# carries the real shapes (adaProductShape and friends). If geochemProduct ever gains root
# requirements, delete this marker and write the shape.
